<div class="Story">
<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Base (LiveComponent — delivery address, no company)</h4>
    <p class="Story-label">
        Empty here: the component fills itself from an <code>addressId</code> the checkout in
        progress is entitled to see, and the toolkit has none. Log in on the front office and pass
        an identifier to preview an address being edited.
    </p>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Forms:Address:Base />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Base with <code>withCompany</code> (billing address)</h4>
    <p class="Story-label">
        The company name only belongs to the billing address, and the legal identifiers come with
        it: they appear once a company name is typed.
    </p>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Forms:Address:Base :withCompany="true" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Account (the same form on the account address book)</h4>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Forms:Address:Account />
    </div>
</div>
</div>
